# Cloud first

Run tool calls in Cursor Cloud (sky icon, managed Ubuntu VM) unless the task
explicitly needs files, GPU, iOS tools, or credentials that exist only on one
Mac.

Best practice is that routing — not local scripts.

- Stay on **Cursor Grok 4.6 High**. Other Models / on-demand is exhausted —
  do not switch to Claude, GPT, Gemini, or a computerUse subagent.
- Exactly one worker registration per physical Mac. Never two on the same
  `machineId`.
- Do not target `mac-mini`. NEVER. It drops its connection and orphans
  runs. `eligibleForSubagent: true` is CONN-CHURN, not a Task target.
- Do not spawn Task subagents to Mini or the Air. They ERROR or boot
  Linux `hostname: cursor`.
- Lille MacBook Air is 8 GB and swap-bound. Not a Cloud target now.
  Prefer Cloud. Do not Task, apply, or kickstart there. Mini is not
  overflow. Delete nothing without Viggo's yes.
- `lille-macbook-air` is desktop-only, and not while it is memory-starved.
  `eligibleForSubagent: true` on the Air is not a Cloud target.
- Do not open `~/cursor` / `viggo-1/cursor` as a Cursor window while the
  launchd worker runs. That spawns `~/cursor @ Lille MacBook Air` on the
  same `machineId` and evicts the hardened worker.
- Never target `~/cursor @ …`, `~/code @ …`, or `cursor-agent-worker-*`.
- Do not start from Save or `CURSOR_API_KEY`. A committed
  `.cursor/environment.json` is enough for Cloud Agents.
- Private Cloud clones need the Cursor GitHub App on the repo org.
  `skoenheden` and `Boom-Butik` both have it (`contents:write`).
  Boom-Butik install: target_id=142605033
  https://github.com/organizations/Boom-Butik/settings/installations/159280535

stop-stray / forget-app / watchdog-hooks are temporary patches for product
gaps (My Machines has no Delete). They are not the goal. Do not add more
unless something is on fire.
